-- =====================================================================
-- MillProof: EXPANDED DEMO DATA (idempotent, safe to re-run)
-- 17 fictional sellers at real North American industrial-city coordinates,
-- 44 synthetic certificates (chemistry within each grade's published limits),
-- 74 active listings across all 10 grades in the reference library.
-- Every seller is labeled "(Synthetic Demo)". Prices are illustrative, not market quotes.
-- Uses its own ID ranges (a1/a2/a3...), so existing rows are not touched.
--
-- Works on both the canonical schema and databases that still carry legacy prototype columns
-- (e.g. sellers.headquarters_city NOT NULL): rows are staged in temp tables, then copied using
-- only the columns that exist, with required legacy columns filled from city/state/country.
--
-- Run in Supabase: SQL Editor -> New query -> paste ALL of this -> Run. (Works statement-by-statement.)
-- =====================================================================
-- Everything below runs as ONE statement (a DO block), so it works even when the SQL editor
-- executes statements one at a time / without a shared transaction.
DO $do$
